                ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text iZsmbxAyAQ9kTuiLe"><p>2020</p></div
                ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text i4vjYeAL9NgdlRPF0"><p>The question that changed everything</p></div
                ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text ihLnbMPLI1KvgcWYD"
                  ><p>Late one night in Amsterdam, watching someone I loved reach for their habit for the hundredth time that day, I realized something.</p><p></p><p>Everyone was focused on the nicotine. The patches. The gum. The willpower. But what if the real dependency wasn&apos;t chemical, it was ritual?</p><p></p><p>The hand-to-mouth motion. The pause. The breath.</p><p>The moment of escape repeated thousands of times until it becomes automatic.</p><p></p><p><em>What if we&apos;re solving the wrong problem?</em></p></div
                ></div
              ></div
            ></div
          ></div
        ></div
      ></div
